<title>INDONESIA: Astra International says 9-mth net up.</title>
<headline>Astra International says 9-mth net up.</headline>
<dateline>JAKARTA 1996-11-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Nine months to September 30</p>
<p>			 (in billion rupiah unless stated)</p>
<p>Non-financial services</p>
<p>    Total revenues			  9,058.54  vs 8,794.98</p>
<p>    Gross profit			    1,690.22  vs 1,591.01</p>
<p>    Operating income			  828.75  vs   856.56</p>
<p>    Pre-tax profit			    435.34  vs   452.81</p>
<p>Financial services</p>
<p>    Total revenues			    936.97  vs   643.75</p>
<p>    Expenses				    753.64  vs   482.51</p>
<p>    Pre-tax profit			    183.32  vs   161.25</p>
<p>Consolidated results</p>
<p>    Total pre-tax profit		    618.67  vs   614.06</p>
<p>    Income before minority interest     453.40  vs   415.73</p>
<p>    Net profit				  340.85  vs   271.41</p>
<p>    Retained earnings		     1,409.78  vs 1,074.05</p>
<p>    Earnings per share (rupiah)		391  vs   311</p>
<p>Note: The consolidated results were unaudited. PT Astra International is one of Indonesia's largest groups, with interests ranging from vehicle assembly and financial services to agribusiness.</p>
<p>-- Jakarta newsroom +6221 384-6364</p>
</text>
